 fission yeast cell cycle: Quantized cycle times in wee1-cdc25 mutant cells.</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><volume>97(14)</volume><fpage>7865</fpage><lpage>7870</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10884416</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001672-Tyson2"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tyson</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>KC</given-names></name><name><surname>Novak</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Network dynamics and cell physiology.</article-title><source>Nature Rev Mol Cell Biol</source><volume>2</volume><fpage>908</fpage><lpage>916</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11733770</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001672-Braunewell1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Braunewell</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Bornholdt</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Superstability of the yeast cell-cycle dynamics: Ensuring causality in the presence of biochemical stochasticity.</article-title><source>J Theor Biol</source><volume>245(4)</volume><fpage>638</fpage><lpage>643</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17204290</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001672-Albert1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Albert</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Othmer</surname><given-names>HG</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>The topology of the regulatory interactions predicts the expression pattern of the Drosophila segment polarity genes.</article-title><source>J Theor Biol</source><volume>223</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>18</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12782112</pub-id></citation></ref><